# Implementation Plan: Student Account Creation Flow & Self-Signup

## Overview
Change the student admission workflow so admins create the student admission record without creating a user account upfront. Students then self-signup via a secure, two-step verification and completion flow (`/student-signup` -> `/student-signup/complete`), auto-logging them into their dashboard upon completion.

---

## Proposed Changes

### Backend (`server/`)

#### [MODIFY] [`Student.model.js`](file:///d:/school%20erp/server/src/models/Student.model.js)
- Add `name: { type: String, required: [true, "Student name is required"], trim: true }`
- Add `isAccountActivated: { type: Boolean, default: false, index: true }`
- Add `signupTokenUsed: { type: Boolean, default: false }`
- Make `userId` optional (`default: null`, remove `required`, use `sparse: true`)

#### [MODIFY] [`student.controller.js`](file:///d:/school%20erp/server/src/controllers/student.controller.js)
- Update `createStudentSchema`: Remove `email` and `password` requirements; require `name`, `admissionNumber`, `dob`, `classId`.
- Update `createStudent`: Only create the `Student` record (no `User` created at this point). `isAccountActivated: false`, `userId: null`.
- Send admission notification email via Resend to `guardianEmail` (if provided) with admission number, DOB instruction, and link to `/student-signup`.
- Update `listStudents`: Fix aggregate pipeline `$unwind` with `preserveNullAndEmptyArrays: true` so pending-activation students show in the admin list; search by `name` or `userInfo.name`.
- Update `updateStudent`: Handle case where `student.userId` is null (update `student.name` directly).

#### [NEW] [`studentSignup.controller.js`](file:///d:/school%20erp/server/src/controllers/studentSignup.controller.js)
- `verifyStudentSignup`:
  - Input: `{ admissionNumber, dob }`
  - Find Student by `admissionNumber` (case-insensitive trim).
  - Verify `dob` matches (date-only comparison).
  - Return generic 400 `"Invalid admission number or date of birth"` if no match or DOB mismatch.
  - Return 409 `"Account already activated. Please login instead."` if `isAccountActivated` is true.
  - Sign short-lived JWT `signupToken` (15m expiry) with `SIGNUP_TOKEN_SECRET` containing `{ studentId: student._id }`.
  - Return `{ signupToken, studentName: student.name }`.
- `completeStudentSignup`:
  - Input: `{ signupToken, email, password }`
  - Verify `signupToken` using `SIGNUP_TOKEN_SECRET`.
  - Validate password strength: min 8 characters, at least one number.
  - Check `isAccountActivated` is still false (race condition protection).
  - Check `email` is not already used by another `User`.
  - Create new `User` with role `"student"`, `name = student.name`, `schoolId`, hashed password.
  - Update `Student` record: `userId = newUser._id`, `isAccountActivated = true`, `signupTokenUsed = true`.
  - Send welcome email via Resend.
  - Issue access + refresh tokens, set `refreshToken` cookie, return `{ user, accessToken, redirectTo: "/student/dashboard" }`.

#### [NEW] [`studentSignup.routes.js`](file:///d:/school%20erp/server/src/routes/studentSignup.routes.js)
- Express router with:
  - `POST /verify`: Rate-limited aggressively (5 attempts per 15 min per IP via `express-rate-limit`).
  - `POST /complete`: Public endpoint, validates token and creates account.
- Explicitly documented as public pre-auth routes (no `authMiddleware`).

#### [MODIFY] [`auth.routes.js`](file:///d:/school%20erp/server/src/routes/auth.routes.js) & [`app.js`](file:///d:/school%20erp/server/src/app.js)
- Mount `studentSignup.routes.js` under `/student-signup` (accessible at `/api/auth/student-signup/*`).

